[4] - Game-based proove are not formal enough (review 3)
R3: "Original Sphinx uses formal game-based definition. This paper does describe games for unlinkability and integrity tag unforgeability, but these are very informal arguments and ultimately still heuristic analysis.
For example, the threat model assumes an adversary cannot break certain computational assumptions, rather than showing a reduction from the proposed game to the underlying hardness assumptions."
